## Facts & Assumptions

**Given:** Full AC and the two displayed oriented knot Seifert matrices in the positive-push convention.

[A1] Full AC is the ambient hypothesis for the Seifert pairing. [[def-axiom-of-choice]]

[F1] The trefoil matrix $V_T$ is the positive-push matrix for the positive trefoil. [[ex-knot-kt-06-worked-cases]]

[F2] The figure-eight matrix $V_F$ is a positive-push Seifert matrix; its skew part is the standard symplectic block. [[def-knot-seifert-pairing-and-matrix]], [[lem-seifert-matrix-skew-part-is-surface-intersection]]

[F3] The Arf invariant is $q(a)q(b)$ for a genus-one symplectic basis and equals $a_2$ modulo two. [[def-knot-arf-invariant-from-seifert-form]], [[thm-arf-equals-second-conway-coefficient-mod-two]]

## Proof

1.1 Since $1-(-1)=2$, $H_{-1}(V)=2(V+V^T)$. For the trefoil, $V_T+V_T^T=\begin{psmallmatrix}2&-1\\-1&2\end{psmallmatrix}$ has eigenvalues $1,3$, so the signature is $2$. For the figure-eight, $V_F+V_F^T=\begin{psmallmatrix}2&-1\\-1&-2\end{psmallmatrix}$ has determinant $-5<0$, hence one positive and one negative eigenvalue, so the signature is $0$. [A1, F1, F2, given, determinant, eigenvalue count]

2.1 The standard intersection block is $\begin{psmallmatrix}0&1\\-1&0\end{psmallmatrix}$ for both matrices. The quadratic values on the basis vectors are their diagonal entries modulo two, namely $(1,1)$ for each matrix. Therefore $\operatorname{Arf}=1\cdot1=1$ for each knot. Their Alexander determinants are $\det(V_T-tV_T^T)=1-t+t^2$ and $\det(V_F-tV_F^T)=-1+3t-t^2$. Substituting $t^{1/2}-t^{-1/2}=z$ with the symmetric normalization gives $\nabla_T=1+z^2$ and $\nabla_F=1-z^2$; both $z^2$ coefficients are odd, agreeing with the Arf values. [F1, F2, F3, step 1.1, determinant, algebra] ∎
